# Binaries
# `go build ./...` at the repo root emits a binary named after the module
# (github.com/serkanalgur/termmosaic -> ./termmosaic). The example main
# packages build into their own directory, and can also be emitted at the
# root with -o, so both locations are covered.
/termmosaic
/hello
/markets
/examples/*/dashboard
/examples/*/hello
/examples/*/markets
# Conventional Go output directory. Nothing in the repo writes to it today,
# but it is the default install/bin target for future release tooling.
/bin/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store